2010/10/15 Jorge Llamb=EDas <jjllambias@gmail.com>:

> Questions are (which is always strange, but anyway)

Not at all strange.  Any point in a jufra may be the one being
queried, just as ma, mo, and the like may appear anywhere in a jufra
but cause the whole jufra to be a question.

> but "xu kau" isn't.  Otherwise, how would we do indirect questions?

You're right about that; my bad.

In any case, I generally object to "parsimonious ontologies" (pc's
phrase) that map the types of objects that fall into the x1 place of a
NU selbri into one another.  Truth values are not necessarily to be
identified with quantities (though, to answer another question, a
quantity can be used anywhere a number is wanted), and neither of them
with propositions.

